# ---- add-ons app: relative paths resolved (found live 13/08 by Mark's audit) ----
# The app's own HTML uses RELATIVE paths - `assets/hero-091-1200.webp`,
# `shared/analytics-addons.js` - because on its subdomain deployment it sits at
# the site root, where those resolve correctly.
#
# Served here at /add-ons-exclusive-discount-938476, the browser resolves them
# against the VISIBLE url, which is at the root of the main domain. So they land
# on the main site's /assets/ and /shared/, where the files do not exist: ten
# broken images and a dead analytics script.
#
# Netlify serves an existing static file BEFORE applying a rule without the `!`
# force flag, so these are pure fallbacks. The main site's own assets are
# untouched; only a path with no file behind it falls through to the app's
# folders. Verified: of 38 add-ons assets, the only filename shared with the
# main site is hero-196-1200.webp, and the two are the same photograph.
#
# The tidier long-term fix is to 301 these three routes to the subdomain, which
# removes the duplicate app entirely. Not done here because the subdomain could
# not be reached to confirm it serves these exact paths, and this is a live site.
/shared/analytics-addons.js   /addons/shared/analytics-addons.js   200   # exclude
/assets/*                     /addons/assets/:splat                200   # exclude
# Affiliate pages: edge function memory-catcher injects per-franchisee data into the our-kit template
/memory-catcher/*   /keepsake-standalone.html   200   # exclude

